The AMD rendering profile globally selects Zink for GBM. Mesa's VA loader
inherits that override too, but the separate JPEG-only driver contains
RadeonSI, not Zink. Clear it only in the USB camera service so VA detects
the DRM device normally; keep desktop rendering and SELinux unchanged.
Drop when renderer selection no longer leaks into the VA loader.

--- a/etc/init/android.hardware.camera.provider-usb-service.android-desktop.rc
+++ b/etc/init/android.hardware.camera.provider-usb-service.android-desktop.rc
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
     interface aidl android.hardware.camera.provider.ICameraProvider/usb/0
     class hal
     user cameraserver
+    setenv MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE ""
     group audio camera input drmrpc usb
     ioprio rt 4
     capabilities SYS_NICE
